1:["$","$Ld",null,{"page":{"id":"library--speaking-with-partner","kind":"library-article","route":"/roadmap/library/speaking-with-partner","sourceUrl":"https://refold.la/roadmap/library/speaking-with-partner","sourceHash":"71f4232b9c753da24e93d7aefd4118f6c9053f0e5c6047209f444fc388068215","collectedAt":"2026-09-01T23:11:06.170Z","bodyMode":"authorized-full-body","title":{"en":"Speaking with Partner","zh":"与搭档练习口语"},"description":{"en":"","zh":""},"segments":[{"id":"segment-0001","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Speaking with a partner means having a real conversation with another person in the target language. It can be a tutor, a language exchange partner, a friend, a family member, or anyone willing to talk.","zh":"与搭档练习口语是指用目标语言与另一个人进行真实对话。对方可以是导师、语言交换伙伴、朋友、家人，或任何愿意和你交谈的人。"}},{"id":"segment-0002","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"We gave it the clunky name \"Speaking with Partner\" to differenciate from Speaking Alone and cover all the bases for different kinds of conversations/language sessions. But it means conversation.","zh":"我们使用了稍显生硬的名称“与搭档练习口语”，是为了将其与独自练习口语区分开来，同时涵盖各种不同形式的对话和语言练习活动。不过，它其实就是指进行对话。"}},{"id":"why-conversation-matters","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Why Conversation Matters","zh":"对话为何重要"}},{"id":"segment-0004","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Conversation is the ultimate test of your language ability — it requires listening comprehension, vocabulary retrieval, grammar under time pressure, pronunciation, and social awareness all at once. It's also the most rewarding part of language learning for most people, because it's <em>real communication</em>.","zh":"对话是对语言能力的终极考验——它要求你同时运用听力理解、词汇提取、时间压力下的语法组织、发音和社交意识。对大多数人来说，这也是语言学习中最有成就感的部分，因为它是<em>真实的交流</em>。"}},{"id":"segment-0005","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"You can practice speaking alone (through monologuing or reading aloud), but conversation adds the element of unpredictability. You can't rehearse what the other person will say, which forces your brain to process and produce language in real-time.","zh":"你可以独自练习口语（例如独白或朗读），但对话增加了不可预测性。你无法预先排练对方会说什么，这会迫使大脑实时处理并产出语言。"}},{"id":"finding-partners","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Finding Partners","zh":"寻找练习搭档"}},{"id":"segment-0007","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"en":"<strong>Paid tutors:</strong> Platforms like iTalki, Preply, or Verbling connect you with professional tutors. This is the most structured option and ideal for getting feedback.","zh":"<strong>付费导师：</strong>iTalki、Preply 或 Verbling 等平台可以帮你联系专业导师。这是最有系统性的选择，也最适合获得反馈。"},{"en":"<strong>Language exchange:</strong> Apps like Tandem, HelloTalk, or conversation exchange websites match you with native speakers who are learning your language.","zh":"<strong>语言交换：</strong>Tandem、HelloTalk 等应用或语言交换网站，可以帮你匹配正在学习你的母语的目标语言母语者。"},{"en":"<strong>Friends and family:</strong> If you know native speakers, just start talking to them.","zh":"<strong>朋友和家人：</strong>如果你认识目标语言的母语者，直接开始和他们交谈即可。"},{"en":"<strong>AI chatbots:</strong> Increasingly good for practice, especially when no human is available. They're patient, always available, and don't judge. But they're not a full replacement for real human interaction.","zh":"<strong>AI 聊天机器人：</strong>它们越来越适合用来练习，尤其是在找不到真人陪练时。它们很有耐心、随时在线，也不会评判你。不过，它们无法完全取代真实的人际互动。"}]},{"id":"tips","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Tips","zh":"实用建议"}},{"id":"segment-0009","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"en":"<strong>Ask questions.</strong> Especially when you're a beginner at speaking, letting the other person talk more gives you time to listen and think. Questions also make the conversation more interesting for both of you.","zh":"<strong>多提问。</strong>尤其是在你刚开始练习口语时，让对方多说一些，可以给你更多时间倾听和思考。提问也能让你们双方都觉得对话更有趣。"},{"en":"<strong>Don't pretend you understood.</strong> If you missed something, ask them to repeat or rephrase. This is a learning opportunity, not a failure.","zh":"<strong>不要假装自己听懂了。</strong>如果漏听了什么，就请对方重复一遍或换个说法。这是一次学习机会，并不意味着失败。"},{"en":"<strong>Don't ask everyone to correct your mistakes.</strong> Most people aren't good at this and find it awkward. If you want correction, hire a tutor for that. In casual conversation, focus on communicating. Live conversations also aren't the best place to apply corrections anyway.","zh":"<strong>不要让每个人都纠正你的错误。</strong>大多数人并不擅长纠错，而且会觉得这样很尴尬。如果你希望有人纠正你，可以专门聘请一位辅导老师。日常对话中，应把重点放在交流上。况且，即时对话本来也不是消化和运用纠正意见的最佳场合。"},{"en":"<strong>Don't expect to be understood perfectly.</strong> You have a foreign accent and make mistakes. That's fine. If someone doesn't understand you, try again with different words. You'll smooth out the issues with practice.","zh":"<strong>不要期待别人能完全听懂你。</strong>你会带有外国口音，也会犯错，这没关系。如果有人没听懂，就换一种说法再试一次。随着练习增多，这些问题会逐渐消失。"},{"en":"<strong>Frequency matters more than duration.</strong> Three 30-minute conversations per week is better than one 90-minute session.","zh":"<strong>频率比时长更重要。</strong>每周进行三次 30 分钟的对话，比只进行一次 90 分钟的对话更有效。"}]},{"id":"when-to-start","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"When to Start","zh":"何时开始"}},{"id":"segment-0011","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Full conversation practice begins in Phase 4B. Before that, crosstalk lets you practice the comprehension side of conversation without the pressure of speaking.","zh":"完整的对话练习从阶段 4B 开始。在此之前，你可以通过交叉谈话练习对话中的理解能力，而不必承受开口说话的压力。"}}],"cards":[]},"siteBasePath":"/my_learning_docs"}]
